<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sirimavo Bandaranaike</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1916–2000</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sirimavo Bandaranaike was a Sri Lankan politician who in 1960 became the world's first woman prime minister, leading the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sri-lanka">Sri Lanka</a> Freedom Party after the assassination of her husband, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/s-w-r-d-bandaranaike">S. W. R. D. Bandaranaike</a>. She served three terms, 1960–1965, 1970–1977 and 1994–2000, nationalising key industries and overseeing the 1972 constitution that made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ceylon">Ceylon</a> the republic of Sri Lanka.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sirimavo-bandaranaike.jpg" alt="Sirimavo Bandaranaike" width="320" height="382" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Indiragandhifan · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bandaranaike_1974.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
